"",""]]},"RC8FS":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"S5DTF":{"d":[["Distribution: Widespread. Blasdale (1957) gave the distribution as Rhodesia, Transvaal, Cape Province and South West Africa. My records extend this to Natal, Zambia, Angola and southern Mozambique. The distribution of P. cineraseens was given by Blasdale (1957) as Tanzania, Malawi, Zambia and northern Mozambique. I have only seen specimens from Malawi (2 ♀, Lauwandi Drift, Shire River, between Zomba & Ft. Johnstone, J. D. Casey (D. M. )) and northern Mozambique (2 6 -, Namalala Stream, 22. XI. J 956 (C. M. & N. M. )), and therefore Blasdale's (1957) distribution records are supported. There is a strong possibility that P. cineraseens will be collected in southern Africa. Prey: Nothing is known concerning the prey of P. tenuipes.","","text","",""]]},"S5WN9":{"d":[["Global","","text","native","endangered"]]},"S9CW":{"d":[["South America","","text","",""]]},"SGPF6":{"d":[["Distribution. Gabon.","","text","",""]]},"SL2SB":{"d":[["Ecuadorian Exclusive Economic Zone (Galapagos)","8403","mrgid","native",""]]},"TC4G4":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"TPQQ":{"d":[["","US","iso","",""],["District of Columbia","","text","",""],["New Mexico","","text","",""]]},"TS6R7":{"d":[["Moldova","48481","mrgid","native",""]]},"TT43W":{"d":[["eastern Amazon River and tributaries (on south bank, west to Río Madeira), and coastal northeastern and eastern Brazil (southward to Rio de Janeiro)","","text","",""]]},"TTR6V":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"V2GKL":{"d":[["Sweden","SE","iso","native","least concern"]]},"VBMNS":{"d":[["Nei Mongol","48041","mrgid","",""]]},"VCFYN":{"d":[["Global","","text","native","critically endangered"]]},"WH9N":{"d":[["","ZM","iso","",""]]},"X2BZ":{"d":[["China (Yunnan)","","text","",""]]},"X2C9":{"d":[["Western and Northern Madagascar","22035","mrgid","",""]]},"ZFSS":{"d":[["Sahul Shelf","21727","mrgid","",""]]},"ZJKW":{"d":[["Jamaica","","text","",""]]},"ZJL6":{"d":[["Dominican Republic